    ],
    "text": "An Exploration of Music Evolution Based on In\ufb02uencer"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0002-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Network and Cosine Similarity"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Aiming to comprehend the evolution of music, we combine the network science, cosine similarity, Cooling Model and Gravity Model in physics, as well as other sta- tistical methods to explore how music evolves through in\ufb02uence across artists and genres."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Above all, we created the directed in\ufb02uencer network to visualize the relationship between in\ufb02uencers and followers. We then explain the concept of music in\ufb02uence with the help of the Cooling Model to describe one\u2019s declining in\ufb02uence as the time interval gets longer. Having done that, we show the music in\ufb02uence of artists in a subnetwork by the size of nodes and conduct detailed analysis."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003",
      "p0001-n0014-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Next, after data pre-processing, we use PCA to reduce the dimensionality of music characteristics and extract four factors. Based on the eigenvector formed by the four factors, we calculate cosine similarity between artisits or genres. Our method to mea- sure similarity proves to be right since artists within genres get higher similarity than artists between genres."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Then, we develop our basic model of network and similarity to solve tasks about the evolution of music.Our analysis is from the following four perspectives."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001",
      "p0001-n0016-l0002",
      "p0001-n0016-l0003",
      "p0001-n0016-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For tasks about in\ufb02uencers and followers, we compare the similarity density curve between followers and in\ufb02uencers or non-in\ufb02uencers and af\ufb01rm the in\ufb02uencers\u2019 im- pact on followers music. Then, we rebuild the eigenvector to calculate similarity by removing each characteristic to see which one is more contagious during the in\ufb02uence process of a particular genre."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0001",
      "p0001-n0017-l0002",
      "p0001-n0017-l0003",
      "p0001-n0017-l0004",
      "p0001-n0017-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For tasks about trends of genres, \ufb01rstly we calculate the similarity matrix of genres and describe relations and difference between genres accordingly. Next, based on the Gravity Model, we estimate the dominant genre of each year and analyze the trends of genres changing over time. In addition, we analyze the evolution of country mu- sic particularly by using popularity and counts to \ufb01gure out dynamic in\ufb02uencer and explain the fusion of country and other genres during its evolution."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0001",
      "p0001-n0018-l0002",
      "p0001-n0018-l0003",
      "p0001-n0018-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For tasks about musical revolutions, we analyze the cosine similarity between each year and its following year to identify signi\ufb01cant changes as revolutions. We \ufb01nd that the periods of the 1940s, 1960s and 1980s are revolutionary period and we particularly anaylze the revolution between 1965 and 1967 to \ufb01nd out the Beatles and Bob Dylan are two artists represent revolution in this periods."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000021",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0019-l0000",
      "p0001-n0019-l0001",
      "p0001-n0019-l0002",
      "p0001-n0019-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For tasks about other impacts of music evolution, we give a detailed analysis on the genre timeline and revolution period with major cultural, social, political or tech- nological changes, explaining how events like the Cold War, Civil Rights Movements in\ufb02uenced the evolution of music."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000022",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0020-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0000",
      "p0001-n0020-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "To summarize, our models have enlightening values for further study due to its comprehensiveness, innovation and good performace in sensitive analysis."
  },
